      "text": "For all real Delta mu, a, sigma > 0, the critical radius rStar = 2 a sigma / (3 Delta mu) is positive, G(r) <= G(rStar) for every r >= 0 where G(r) = -Delta mu r^3 + a sigma r^2, and any r >= 0 with G(r) = G(rStar) equals rStar. For all Delta mu > 0 and all real a, sigma, G(rStar) = (1/2) Delta mu rStar^3.",
      "trivial": false
    },
    "C2": {
      "kind": "conjecture",
      "label": "ASSUMED",
      "reason": "conjecture",
      "text": "Observation from a local check, not a sealed claim: the half-barrier identity G(rStar) = (1/2) Delta mu rStar^3 holds for every real Delta mu (for Delta mu = 0 by Lean's x/0 = 0 convention), so the hypothesis 0 < Delta mu in part (ii) of P2.Restoration is not used mathematically."
